EtherCAT/Pci1203Control.h: kCmdRingReset appended LAST to the kind enum (value = ring mask 1 / 2 / 3); Acm_MasResetRing(HAND, U16 RingNo) added to the allowlist. Pci1203Control.cpp (all same-line): validation (mask 1..3), no axis handle needed, runs on the IO thread BETWEEN two polls and is adopted at once (like kCmdCardRescan), wire name pci1203.ring.reset both ways, parse needs the mask. Live: Acm_MasResetRing bound with GetProcAddress (not in AdvMotApi.h; the import lib only carries a C++-mangled name; signature from the vendor C# wrapper AdvMotAPI.dll), each ring in the mask; all OK -> TPci1203Monitor::RescanRing; a missing export, no device handle or a failed reset (this card's Mas* family answered 0x80000005 on 9/12) -> Rescan(). Pci1203Monitor: RescanRing (close axis handles, re-scan slaves, re-open axes on the SAME device handle, publish) -- no vendor write; readonly gate and control gate both PASS.

Not wired yet (stage 3 = wb_serve triggers / stop conditions / WAR16150 / WAR16157 / after-recovery steps). Tests: Pci1203Pure 106/106 (+4: name both ways, wire parse with / without mask, refused on a closed control), Pci1203Reopen 22/22, Pci1203LinkWatch / ModuleCheck / MotorRoute pass. Debug + release (affected targets).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
